First, we note that the given equation is in base $b$.  We can rewrite the equation in base $10$ as follows:

\begin{align*}
5_b \cdot 23_b &= 151_b \\
5b + 3 &= 1b^2 + 5b + 1 \\
0 &= b^2 - 2b - 2 \\
0 &= (b - 4)(b + 1)
\end{align*}

Therefore, we have $b - 4 = 0$ or $b + 1 = 0$.  Since we want a positive base, we must have $b = 4$.

